## 6. Authentication & Authorization

### Permission Checking Pattern

**ALWAYS use helper methods, not direct role checks:**

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT
if (auth.canAdmin) {
  // Admin-only logic
}

if (auth.canOperate) {
  // Operator or Admin logic
}

// ❌ WRONG
if (auth.hasRole(['admin'])) { }
if (auth.hasRole(['admin', 'operator'])) { }
```

**Reason:** Helper methods provide semantic clarity and can be updated centrally if role logic changes.

### User-Specific Endpoints Pattern

```javascript
// Pattern: /:username/resource
router.get(
  '/:username/sessions',
  isPermittedTo('read', { checkOwnership: true }),
  asyncHandler(async (req, res) => {
    const username = req.params.username;
    
    // Ownership check happens in middleware
    const sessions = await prisma.genome_browser_session.findMany({
      where: { user: { username } }
    });
    
    res.json({ sessions });
  })
);
```

### Cookie-Based File Access

For genome browser file serving:

```javascript
// 1. Set cookie
router.post('/:id/set-file-cookie', async (req, res) => {
  const token = jwt.sign(
    { user_id: req.user.id, session_id: req.params.id },
    JWT_SECRET,
    { expiresIn: '1h' }
  );
  
  res.cookie('bioloop_session_token', token, {
    httpOnly: true,
    secure: true,
    sameSite: 'lax',
    maxAge: 3600000,
  });
  
  res.json({ success: true });
});

// 2. Authenticate with cookie
const authenticateWithCookie = asyncHandler(async (req, res, next) => {
  const token = req.cookies.bioloop_session_token;
  if (!token) throw createError(401, 'Token not found');
  
  const decoded = jwt.verify(token, JWT_SECRET);
  
  if (decoded.session_id !== parseInt(req.params.id)) {
    throw createError(403, 'Token does not match session');
  }
  
  req.user = await prisma.user.findUnique({
    where: { id: decoded.user_id }
  });
  
  next();
});
```

